SUMMARY:Seed and Soul Club’s Fall Swap
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
DTSTAMP:20261017T204148Z
UID:funcheap-1638299@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Outdoors
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerZeldric TamayoJoin the Seed an
 d Soul Club for our last plant swap in San Francisco for 2026! This time\,
  we’re heading to City College of San Francisco’s Horticulture and Flo
 ristry Department. You’ll get to learn from the department’s instructo
 rs\, explore their greenhouses\, and enjoy some of Julia’s delicious pie
 s.\nWe’re also teaming up with the department to spread the word about t
 heir free classes for San Francisco residents. If you’ve ever wanted to 
 go deeper than a swap\, this is where to start.\n\nEvent Highlights:\n\nTh
 e Signature SSC Plant Swap. Bring a healthy plant\, leave with a new one. 
 Our coordinated exchange is built so everyone goes home with something the
 y’re excited about.New to this? Read our process before you come.\nPick 
 Your Plant Adventure. Choose one: take a self-guided tour of the City Coll
 ege greenhouses\, sit in on a horticulture or floristry class happening th
 at day\, or watch a demo on mounting epiphytes\nCCSF Plant Sale. The depar
 tment will be selling plants on-site\, and every purchase goes toward mate
 rials and supplies for their classes.\nJulia’s Pies Is Back. Our favorit
 e pie stand returns\, so plan your slice around the swap.\nCommunity Impac
 t. Leftover plants from the swap go straight to the CCSF Horticulture Depa
 rtment’s programs and students’ classwork\, so your plants keep teachi
 ng long after the swap ends.\n\nTo participate in our signature swap\, adv
 ance registration is required. Spots are limited for a seamless experience
 \,...\n\n$20.00\n\nTickets: https://www.seedandsoulclub.org/upcoming-swaps
 /fallswap2026\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/seed-soul-clubs-fall-swap/
 \nSource: Funcheap SF
