DESCRIPTION:Bay Area Science Festival 2026\nSaturday\, October 17 | Koret 
 Quad\, UCSF Mission Bay Campus\n\nDiscover science fun and excitement toge
 ther at the Bay Area Science Festival — Northern California’s largest 
 free\, all-ages science event. Experience 125+ mind-blowing hands-on exper
 iments\, games\, demonstrations\, stage performances\, film screenings and
  science talks. Bring the whole family to race robots\, see your own brain
 waves\, participate in a science podcast\, marvel at science magic shows\,
  meet reptiles and amphibians face-to-face and much more.\n\nOrganized by 
 the UCSF Science & Health Education Partnership\, BASF takes place on Satu
 rday\, October 17\, from 11AM-4PM at UCSF’s Mission Bay Campus amid Kore
 t Quad’s expansive lawns\, walkways\, pine grove and renowned educationa
 l\, medical and biotech research facilities — one block from Chase Cente
 r! Rain or shine\, with plenty of indoor and outdoor activities for all ag
 es.\n\nNorthern California's Largest Free Celebration of Science\nThe 13th
  edition brings together STEM role models\, families\, youth and adults to
  experience the wonder of science\, inspire future scientists\, and explor
 e how STEM shapes the way we live.\n\nThe Science & Health Education Partn
 ership at UCSF organizes BASF in collaboration with Bay Area universities\
 , museums\, cultural institutions\, libraries\, corporations\, after-schoo
 l groups\, research labs and government agencies.\n\nLearn more at BayArea
 ScienceFestival.org.\n\nFree\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/
 10/17/bay-area-science-festival-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed o
 n:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/bay-area-science-festival-ucsf/
