BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filipino American Int’l Book Festival 2026 at SF Main Library (O
 ct. 17-18)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T171500
DTSTAMP:20261007T210655Z
UID:funcheap-1641527@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:Filipino American Int’l Book Festival 2026 at SF Main Librar
 y (Oct. 17-18)\nN/A\nThe Filipino American International Book Festival (Fi
 lBookFest)\, presented in partnership with San Francisco Public Library\, 
 returns SFPL’s Main Library for its 8th iteration\, continuing its legac
 y as the largest Filipino American literary festival in the U.S. This year
 ’s theme\, “SANGGALAN: Stories that propel us\, stories that protect u
 s\,” centers stories that carry us forward and hold us together: stories
  as refuge\, stories as resistance\, stories as action.\nHeld during Filip
 ino American History Month\, FilBookFest brings together writers\, scholar
 s\, and creatives from across the globe\, including the U.S.\, Canada\, an
 d the Philippines\, to the iconic San Francisco Public Library. Over two d
 ays\, attendees can enjoy panel discussions\, book signings\, and readings
  featuring a vibrant mix of established and emerging voices. The festival 
 celebrates storytelling\, culture\, and the diverse experiences of the Fil
 ipino diaspora.\nFESTIVAL MARKETPLACE\n\n📍 Latino Room\n11:00 AM – 5:
