DESCRIPTION:Clement Street Art Fair & Broke-Ass Stuart Day\nSaturday\, Oct
 ober 17 |\nClement St btwn. 6th & 8th Ave\n\nRemember last year when the S
 an Francisco Board of Supervisors officially declared October 17th as Brok
 e-Ass Stuart Day? Yeah\, that was pretty cool.\n\nAnd the party that we th
 rew was epic!\n\nWell\, we’ve decided to make it a yearly event and this
  time we’re teaming up with the folks over at the Clement Street Art Fai
 r to do something truly wonderful.\nClement St. Art Fair & Broke-Ass Stuar
 t Day\n\nI’m joining forces with The Clement Street Merchants Associatio
 n and WorkshopSF for the 2nd Annual Broke-Ass Stuart Day and the 3rd annua
 l Clement Street Art Fair.\n\nRSVP Right Here!\n\nClement Street – from 
 6th to 8th Avenues – will close to traffic to provide a fun-filled day o
 f art activations\, live music\, local makers\, and community building. Th
 e event will be hosted by Clement Street Merchants Association and I will 
 emcee!\n\nIt’s all going down on October 17th from 12:00 PM to 5:00 PM a
 nd will offer a ton of fun activities for people of all ages:\nMusical Per
 formances:\n\nSweet Lew\n\nPlovver\n\nSWISS.\n\nEmily Afton\n\nArtist Acti
 vations:\nMake-and-take crafts by Workshop SF\n\nDIY Postcards & Love Lett
 ers to Clement by Risa Iwasaki Culbertson and Leah Jachimowicz of Coffee n
  Cream Press\n\nLive screen printing by Fleetwood\n\nCommunity Art Project
  by Kate Campbell\n\nFeatured Artist:\n\nHollis Callas (Designed SF's "I V
 oted!" stickers and this year’s poster)\n\nPlus there will be food\, dri
 nks\, activities for...\n\nFree\nThe Clement Street Merchants Association\
 , Broke-Ass Stuart + Workshop SF Present\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/
 events/2026/10/17/broke-ass-stuart-day-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso l
 isted on:\n- https://data.sf.gov/d/8x25-yybr\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/to
 p-hill-festival-2026-daly-city/\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/2nd-annual-brok
 eass-stuart-day-sfs-clement-street-art-fair-2026/
