BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jean-Baptiste Phou: Coming Out of My Skin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T203000
DTSTAMP:20261017T204148Z
UID:funcheap-1642738@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerHeadshots submitted to Litquak
 e by participantsPart of Litquake’s Words Around the World\nSponsored by
  Center for the Art of Translation\nCo-presented with Villa Albertine\nHav
 ing grown up as a Cambodian immigrant in France\, Jean-Baptiste Phou has l
 ong explored the challenges and contradictions of the Asian diaspora exper
 ience throughout his artistic career. However\, up until now\, he’s alwa
 ys been careful not to raise issues of sexuality—in particular\, his hom
 osexuality. In his recent memoir\, Coming Out of My Skin\, the artist shif
 ts his focus to examining the role his ethnic origin has played in the con
 struction of his sexual identity and his romantic relationships in a predo
 minantly white environment. An astute observer of the various ways in whic
 h his body has been perceived\, Phou asks: how does a marginalized person 
 develop emotionally and build\, reclaim\, and express their sexuality? How
  does this inform the experience of a queer Asian person navigating predom
 inantly white cultural spaces? In conversation with César Cadabes\, Artis
 tic Director for the GLBTQ Asian Pacific Alliance (GAPA) Theatre. Doors at
  6:30pm\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/jean-baptiste-pho
 u-coming-out-of-my-skin-tickets-1999616387443?aff=oddtdtcreator&amp\;keep_
 tld=true\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/jeanbaptiste-phou-coming-skin/\
 nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/7_10_1
 7-Jean-Baptiste-Phou-IG.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T204148Z
LOCATION:Telegraph Hill Books\, 1501 Grant Avenue\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/jeanbaptiste-phou-coming-skin/
END:VEVENT
