DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSan Francisco Chamber Orchestr
 aProgram:\nLudwig van Beethoven – Coriolan Overture\, Op. 62\nGrace Will
 iams – Sea Sketches\nLudwig van Beethoven – Symphony No. 3 in Eb Major
 \, Op. 55 “Eroica”\n\nBetrayed by Napoleon’s thirst for power\, Beet
 hoven furiously tore apart his 3rd Symphony’s dedication\, and in doing 
 so created a work that captured\, like no other\, the defiant and life-aff
 irming heroic spirit. With its massive size and emotional power\, the Eroi
 ca Symphony would change the course of Classical music forever.\nOur progr
 am begins with the Coriolan Overture\, Beethoven’s electrifying portrait
  of Shakespeare’s doomed warrior followed by Grace William’s hauntingl
 y beautiful Sea Sketches\, which paint the Welsh coastline in all its wild
 \, shimmering glory.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/main
 stage-1-beethovens-eroica-a-heros-journey-tickets-1991879386866?aff=oddtdt
 creator&amp\;keep_tld=true\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/mainstage-1-b
 eethovens-eroica-heros-journey-2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
