DESCRIPTION:“Shipyard Open Studios” Fall 2026: 130+ Artists\, Free Adm
 ission & Parking\nShipyard Trust for the Arts\nShipyard Trust for the Arts
  and ArtSpan teamed up to bring you the fall edition of Shipyard Open Stud
 ios x S F Open Studio event.\nOver 130 artists\, food\, a Beer Garden\, li
 ve music and more at the historic Hunters Point Shipyard and Islais Creek 
 studios.\nMost people have never set foot inside Hunters Point Shipyard\, 
 a historic naval base that\, for one weekend\, becomes one of San Francisc
 o’s biggest art events. Step inside the working studios of 130+ painters
 \, sculptors\, jewelers\, ceramicists\, photographers\, and metalworkers. 
 Talk directly with the artists\, watch how the work gets made\, and take h
 ome something original.\nA short drive away\, the satellite studios at Isl
 ais Creek are home to many of the show’s sculptors\, offering a chance t
 o see large-scale work being made in the space where it happens. Well wort
 h adding to your route.\nShipyard Open Studios\nSaturday & Sunday\, Octobe
 r 17-18\, 2026 | 11a-6p\nHunters Point Shipyard (Shipyard Trust for the Ar
 ts)\, 451 Galvez Ave.\, SF\nFREE | RSVP\nFree parking. Muni accessible (19
 \, 15\, 54)\, bike-friendly\, wheelchair accessible.\nWhat To Expect:\n\n1
 30+ open studios – painting\, sculpture\, jewelry\, photography\, cerami
 cs\, metalwork\, and beyond\nSilent art auction – bid on works from part
 icipating artists and support the event\nLive music – jazz and classical
  performances throughout the weekend\nFood & drink – local vendors plus 
 a beer & wine garden...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1
 992234233221/?aff=fc\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/shipyard-open-studi
 os-fall-2026-130-artists-free-admission-parking-2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
