DESCRIPTION:SF Short Film Festival presents:\n\nCALIFORNIA SUITS YOU\n\nA 
 writer\, tasked with interviewing the owner of a store during its grand op
 ening\, finds an album cover that shouldn't exist and becomes determined t
 o find out what that record holds.\n\nCHASE YOUR DREAMS\n\nLed by the flut
 tering allure of a childhood dream\, a dancer embarks on a whimsical\, bre
 athless journey\, a choreography of pursuit\, a a literal\, continuous spr
 int\, moving one beat ahead of the rhythm\, she must fight through a gaunt
 let of detours threatening to derail her from her childhood wish.\n\nLIFE 
 GOES ON\n\nBILL is in end of life care waiting for the sweet release of de
 ath - but unfortunately for him\, he's stuck in an infinite time loop\, ca
 using the day to restart the second his heart stops... A darkly comic yet 
 sweet and hopeful film about enjoying the time you have left and saying th
 e important things to the important people. Starring BAFTA winner David Br
 adley (Harry Potter\, Game of Thrones).\n\nNORMAL KIDS\n\nTeo and Mikey ar
 e inseparable friends - until a small betrayal sparks a fight before their
  school’s year-end show.\n\nSCHIZM\n\nA man grappling with bizarre side 
 effects from losing a loved one\, opens up about his struggle on YouTube\,
  forming an unexpected bond with a young girl.\n\nDERIVE\n\nGuided by post
 humous instructions to release her ex-wife’s ashes\, a reclusive book pu
 blisher embarks on a Surrealist odyssey (a dérive) across New York City\,
  experiencing a series of spontaneous connections along the way that inspi
 re...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/19/sf-short-film-fes
 tival-spontaneous-connections-shorts-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34917169/65aa6825-eea0-492c-bdb4-1be555f15d2d.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T084210Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/19/sf-short-film-festival-spontane
 ous-connections-shorts-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Naza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T223000
DTSTAMP:20261020T084210Z
UID:dothebay-17930207@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:NAZA screens at NEW PEOPLE October 9–11\, and 18. Screenings
  at The Roxie start October 12.\n\nIn secret conversations on the rooftops
  of Tel Aviv at night\, the systems behind Israel’s calculated mass kill
 ing of Palestinian civilians in Gaza are revealed by the people who design
 ed and operated them.\n\nDirectors Note:\n\nWe made this film out of a sen
 se of obligation to use our position as Israeli filmmakers and journalists
  to examine the systems behind the mass killing of Palestinian civilians f
 or which our country is responsible. While filming members of Israel’s m
 ilitary on rooftops at night in Tel Aviv over the past three years\, we fo
 und ourselves asking the very questions that were asked by our grandparent
 s’ generation and throughout the 20th century: how does one group of peo
 ple allow the total dehumanisation of another?\n\nWhat do the inner workin
 gs of such a system look like? Many of the revelations in the film were pu
 blished almost immediately as we learned of them\, in the months following
  the October 7th attacks\, by The Guardian (one of NAZA’s producers)\, i
 n collaboration with reporting partners +972 Magazine and Local Call. The 
 film lets us explore something deeper than we could in our investigative j
 ournalism alone: not only the words being said but also those that are not
  said\, the silence. It is up to all of us to break that silence.\n\n– Y
 uval Abraham and Rachel Szor\n\n“An essential\, devastating documentary
 …there’s no turning away from what’s said\, you simply can’t unkno
 w...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/19/naza-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34836049/c18ee701-2e31-49a6-bbf4-a5c699d6163d.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T084210Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/19/naza-tickets
END:VEVENT
