SUMMARY:Mad Props: A Comedy Breakdown of the California Ballot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T210000
DTSTAMP:20261021T115902Z
UID:dothebay-17952880@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Comedy
DESCRIPTION:Mad Props is a live variety show where Bay Area journalists br
 eak down the decisions on your ballot\, with a little humor along the way.
 \n\nMad Props is a live variety show where Bay Area journalists help you m
 ake sense of the upcoming election — while also having a little fun! In 
 six interactive presentations\, we’ll cover some of the most consequenti
 al decisions this November\, both statewide and here in SF.\n\nCome for a 
 drink and good laugh\, leave with a headstart on your ballot!\n\nYour Host
 \nEli Benton Cohen is the creator of the Mad Props Voter Guide\, in collab
 oration with the San Francisco Standard and KALW. When he’s not reading 
 the state voter guide you threw away\, he’s probably at Berkeley Bowl.\n
 \nThe Governor’s Race\nSophia Garrow is the Comedy Correspondent at the 
 SF Standard. She asked both Becerra and Hilton hard hitting questions like
  what is Mayor of San Francisco’s name\, what is their favorite girls’
  sport\, and should the U.S. provide military aid to Israel. The answers m
 ay surprise you.\n\nProp 40: The Billionaire Tax\nWill Harris and Matt She
 ppard are reporters and producers at Uncuffed\, KALW’s podcast from insi
 de California prisons. Will and Matt have long used comedy to understand l
 ife on the inside\, and are looking forward to training the same wit on bi
 llionaires.\n\nProp 39: Voter ID\nLaura Fitzgerald is a politics reporter 
 at KQED.\n\nProps D\, E\, & F: Mayor Lurie’s Charter Reforms\nJoe Fitzge
 rald Rodriguez is a politics reporter at the San Francisco Standard. His l
 ove of...\n\nFree\nKALW Public Media\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/even
 ts/2026/10/20/mad-props-a-comedy-breakdown-of-the-california-ballot-ticket
 s\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/mad-prop
 s-comedy-breakdown-california-ballot-kalw-sf/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34943365/4581007b-6ab2-414f-bc1c-73d10c6ef4a5.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T115902Z
LOCATION:KALW @ The Warfield Commons\, 988 Market St.\, 9th Fl\, San Franc
 isco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/20/mad-props-a-comedy-breakdown-of
 -the-california-ballot-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Frameline50 Fall Showcase: Tangles
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T210000
DTSTAMP:20261021T115902Z
UID:dothebay-17967617@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Between landing a promotion to cover artist at her queer activ
 ist zine to falling for her impossibly cool girlfriend (Samira Wiley\, The
  Handmaid’s Tale)\, Sarah (Abbi Jacobson\, Broad City) is finally hittin
 g her stride in ‘90s San Francisco. But a trip home to visit her oddball
  family upends everything. Sarah’s mom\, the once-vibrant Midge (Julia L
 ouis-Dreyfus\, Veep)\, isn’t herself — and Sarah’s father (Bryan Cra
 nston\, Breaking Bad) and sister (Beanie Feldstein\, Booksmart) aren’t q
 uite ready to see the concerning shifts.\n\nPulled between her exciting li
 fe in the Bay and being there for her mother\, Sarah tries to find her foo
 ting in a disorienting world — a world where Alzheimer’s disease is sl
 owly eroding Midge’s sense of self. Based on Sarah Leavitt’s graphic n
 ovel and featuring powerhouse performances from its award-winning ensemble
  cast\, which also includes Seth Rogen (The Studio)\, Wanda Sykes\, and Bo
 wen Yang (Fire Island)\, Leah Nelson’s animated directorial debut is an 
 achingly beautiful story of acceptance and a meditation on the relationshi
 ps that shape — and reshape — us.\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/eve
 nts/2026/10/20/frameline50-fall-showcase-tangles-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
