BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tricky FM’s Twin Star Fantasy Record Release w/ EDGAR and Tugboy
 z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T230000
DTSTAMP:20261018T205153Z
UID:funcheap-1642471@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerKenzie AelligTricky FM is the 
 music project and “electronica star” alter ego of Hana Freed. Based ou
 t of San Francisco\, she self produces all her own music\, while being a s
 taple in clubs\, venues and punk bars throughout the Bay Area and beyond. 
 On stage\, Tricky FM is known for her energetic and almost performance-art
  interpretation of the ‘pop star’. At home\, behind her computer\, she
 ’s crafted her own brand of euphoric sounding electronica. Her work cent
 ers on the complex terrain of navigating contemporary womanhood: trust\, i
 ntimacy\, fulfillment and ultimately the relationship with the self. Her 2
 023 debut Peace\, Love\, Unity\, Rave (Cherub Dream Records) arrived from 
 a place of urgency and anger—a sampled-based Ableton-coded reckoning wit
 h the ways misogyny runs through every facet of life. This album led her t
 o share stages with Alice Glass\, Molly Nilsson\, Mechatok\, Otha\, Spelll
 ing\, Salami Rose Joe Louis and more.\nHer forthcoming album Twin Star Fan
 tasy finds Tricky FM on the other side of this reckoning. Where PLUR was f
 orged in chaos\, Twin Star Fantasy was built in stillness. What fantastica
 l things can be brought forth from the seemingly everyday and mundane? Thi
 s album weaves reflections on stability and the relationships that shaped 
 her—an homage to the past\, a document of the present\, and a prayer for
  the future. It shows an artist at the fullness of her potential\, steppin
 g into a sound that she has been perfecting on her own. Hana produc...\n\n
 $17.00\n\nTickets: https://www.thelab.org/projects/2026/10/22/cherub-dream
 -records-x-the-lab-tricky-fm-twin-star-fantasy-edgar\nDetails: https://sf.
 funcheap.com/tricky-fms-twin-star-fantasy-record-release-edgar-tugboyz/\nS
 ource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tricky
 fm-albumrelease8.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261018T205153Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/tricky-fms-twin-star-fantasy-record-release-ed
 gar-tugboyz/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filipiñana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T223000
DTSTAMP:20261023T114720Z
UID:dothebay-17930193@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Director Rafael Manuel in person for introduction and Q&A mode
 rated by Ali El-Sadany\, editor of FilmSlop\, on Saturday\, September 5 (a
 t rush).\n\nPresented by FiliKula\n\nAmid stifling heat and pervasive drou
 ght\, Isabel (Jorrybell Agoto)\, a 17-year-old Ilokana from the rural nort
 h\, works at a posh country club outside Manila\, lining up golf balls for
  powerful men to drive into the verdant horizon. New to the job\, she wand
 ers the immaculate grounds sampling its luxuries as members\, including an
  industrialist and his expatriate niece\, the club president and his pampe
 red wife\, and a slew of Chinese tourists\, engage in a complex dance with
  the club’s doting and subservient staff. But something is rotting benea
 th the pristine fairways of the elite resort\, as Isabel discovers when sh
 e tries to return a mislaid golf club to its patriarchal director\, Dr. Pa
 lanca (Teroy Guzman). The deeper she journeys into its most exclusive corn
 ers\, the closer she gets to the violent truths of the club\, her native P
 hilippines\, and her own past..\n\n“A masterwork…with Filipiñana\, Ma
 nuel opens new vistas in the future of the cinema.” – The New Yorker\n
 \n“An invigorating dose of arch formalism in a sea of mainstream sinceri
 ty\, this is the kind of movie that asks for the viewer’s attention…th
 e angle of a golf club can evoke suspense\, a piece of fruit on the ground
  can feel like a tragedy\, and a casual glance can take your breath away.
 ” – Vulture\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 40m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nRafael
  Manuel\n\nFormat\n\nDCP...\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/1
 0/22/filipinana-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
