SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival | Heathens (World Premier
 e)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T170000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-83f2ba9cc733878d@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:festival,film
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: (650) 724-5544Cont
 act Email: info@unaff.orgCost: 19Link: www.unaff.orgThe 29th United Nation
 s Association Film Festival (UNAFF) screens the world premiere of "Heathen
 s\," directed by Bay Area filmmakers Shawn Hardin and David Cowan\, on Sat
 urday\, Oct. 24\, at Mitchell Park in Palo Alto. "Heathens" follows five A
 mericans who gather at a secluded retreat after rejecting the religious tr
 aditions in which they were raised. Over one weekend\, they confront the c
 hallenges of living openly as nonbelievers and find community\, friendship
  and a renewed sense of identity.The film is followed by a free panel\, "D
 ifferent Faces of Religion.” It begins at 5:10 p.m. UNAFF runs Oct. 15
 –25\, 2026\, with the theme Passion for Change. The festival features fi
 lms on human rights issues like the environment\, women’s rights\, racis
 m\, and peace\, engaging a diverse Bay Area audience.\n\nPublished by KGO\
 nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nS
 ource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:Mitchell Park Community Center 3700 Middlefield Road Palo Alto
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
