DESCRIPTION:Kultivate LabsFor its tenth anniversary\, UNDISCOVERED SF is b
 ringing the night market vibes back for the first time since the pandemic.
  In partnership with Victory Hall\, formerly known as the iconic nightclub
  330 Ritch\, this year’s themes “Golden Hour” and “Made With Mahal
 \,” make an intimate but electric return. With DJ sets by Hoochi\, Vieux
  Carre\, Boogie Brown\, and performance by The Top Chefs of Live on The St
 oop. Then step inside Victory Hall for a special exhibition honoring the h
 istory of 330 Ritch\, the legendary nightclub that once made this block pu
 lse after dark. The event is FREE for all ages and will take place Saturda
 y\, October 24\, 2026\, from 4-10 PM\, on Ritch Street between Townsend an
 d Brannan. The tenth anniversary edition returns the market’s roots to S
 oMa nightlife history\, pairing that legacy with a new generation of vendo
 rs\, chefs\, and makers who have built their businesses through UNDSCVRD S
 F. This year’s curated vendors include food vendors-Mestiza\, Little Ski
 llet\, Senor Sisig\, Cafe 86\, Ube Area\, and more. Retailers include Mala
 ya Botanicals\, Mie Makes\, Native Sol\, Sunkissed Pinay and more.\nPresen
 ted by Kultivate Labs\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.undiscoveredsf.com/\
 nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-10th-anniversary-golden-hour-night-
 market-victory-hall-sf/\nSource: Funcheap SF
