DESCRIPTION:Tommy LauOne of the most anticipated literary nights of the ye
 ar\, San Francisco’s Lit Crawl is a massive\, one-night literary pub cra
 wl through San Francisco’s Mission District that caps off our annual Lit
 quake Festival. Lit Crawl SF brings together 250+ authors\, 50+ events and
  close to 5\,000 fans for the world’s largest free pop-up literary event
 .\nStarted in 2004\, Lit Crawl cultivates a unique\, resonant brand: smart
  and silly\, worldly and wacky\, with events presented in venues usual (ba
 rs\, cafes\, galleries\, and bookstores) and unusual (tattoo parlors\, bar
 bershops\, and laundromats).\n\nSee the Litcrawl Map for 2026\n\nLit Crawl
  SF 2026\nSaturday\, October 24\, 2026 | 5:00pm–9:00pm | Mission Distric
 t | FREE\nTAILGATE EVE\nPage Street Co-working and The Writers Grotto are 
 hosting free pre-Crawl festivities!\n\nLit & Libations at The Writers Grot
 to – 2:30pm–4:00pm – The Writers Grotto | 1663 Mission St\, Ste 602\
 nWant to Read at Lit Crawl? A Pre-Crawl Tailgate – 3:00pm–4:00pm – P
 age Street Co-working | 297 Page St\n\nPHASE 1: 5:00pm–6:00pm\n\nDr. Str
 angebro: How I Learned to Stop Taking and Start Giving a Shit – Martuni
 ’s\, 21+ | 4 Valencia St\nInvisible City: Letters from the Wilderness 
 – St. John the Evangelist Episcopal Church | 1661 15th St\n¡ChALE con e
 so!: Mujeres en Rebeldía – Muddy Waters | 521 Valencia St\nMommy Issues
  – Blondie’s Bar\, 21+ | 540 Valencia St\nWithout a Net: 20 Super-shor
 t\, Uncurated\, Uncensored\, Unrehearsed Pieces\, Freshly Written in the L
 ast Hour – The Drawing Room: Annex | 5...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://ww
 w.litquake.org/litcrawl\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lit-crawl-sf-epi
 c-4hour-roaming-literature-festival-mission/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/102624
 _LitCrawl_byTommyLau_082.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261013T225222Z
LOCATION:All Over San Francisco\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/lit-crawl-sf-epic-4hour-roaming-literature-fes
 tival-mission/
END:VEVENT
