DESCRIPTION:The 29th United Nations Association Film Festival closes on Su
 nday\, Oct. 25\, at Mitchell Park in Palo Alto\, bringing two feature-leng
 th films.\n\nYo (Love is a Rebellious Bird)\, by Bay Area duo Banker White
  and UNAFF alum Anna Fitch\, is an imaginative film explores creativity as
  an outlet for grief and love.\n\nIn the Company of Wolves: An American Jo
 urney\, narrated by Jeff Bridges and directed by Susan Kucera and Jim Swif
 t\, explores how our relationship with animals shaped a nation. Jeff Bridg
 es is also the recipient of the 29th UNAFF Visionary Award.\nhttps://www.i
 ndybay.org/newsitems/2026/10/12/18889273.php\n\nPublished by Indybay\nCont
 ains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetail
