DESCRIPTION:District 8 Candidate Debate 2026: Final Pre-Election Forum (Ca
 stro)District 8 supervisor candidates Darshini Patel\, Michael Nguyen\, an
 d Gary McCoy take part in a final debate before Election Day at 2140 Marke
 t Street\, the former Lucky 13 location – it’s a rare chance to (legal
 ly) go inside the former dive bar that was closed in 2020. The event is co
 -hosted by community organizer Kent Mirkhani\, with drinks available for a
 ttendees.\nOriginal Event Description:\n_District 8 Supervisor Candidate D
 ebate\nSan Francisco’s District 8 includes the Castro\, Noe Valley\, Dia
 mond Heights\, Glen Park\, and parts of Twin Peaks and Mission Dolores.\nS
 un\, Oct 25 | 2140 Market Street\, San Francisco\, 94114 – This is the f
 ormer Lucky 13 spot that closed in 2020. A rare chance to go inside since 
 it closed.\nA Debate That Only District 8 Could Get Away With!\nDoors Open
  @ 7:30pm\nBuy Tickets\nDistrict 8 Supervisor Candidate Debate\nTime & Loc
 ation\nOct 25\, 2026\, 8:00 PM – 9:30 PM\n2140 Market Street\, San Franc
 isco\, 94114\nAbout the event\nThe race for District 8 Supervisor has been
  the story of the season. Catch the final debate before Election Day with 
 candidates Darshini Patel\, Michael Nguyen\, and Gary McCoy.\nBootstraps a
 nd Ladders is proud to be co-hosting this event with our lead host for the
  night and community organizer Kent Mirkhani. There is no one better who k
 nows District 8 in and out than him.\nWorried that the mood will be too he
 avy? Don’t. We’re keeping the tone a bit lighter\, and drinks availabl
 e for...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.bootstrapsandladders.com/event-de
 tails/district-8-supervisor-candidate-debate\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap
