DESCRIPTION:Thank you to everyone who joined us to celebrate Shireen McSpa
 dden at CLC’s annual event on Oct. 1st. Shireen received the Norma Satte
 n Community Service Innovation Award\, which recognizes people who have wo
 rked tirelessly to protect the rights of seniors and people with disabilit
 ies in the spirit of our first board president\, Norma Satten.\nAs Shireen
  reminded us in her remarks\, CLC is about social connection\, which leads
  to healthier outcomes. We see that every day as neighbors build relations
 hips\, share their talents\, support one another\, and strengthen their co
 mmunities.\nThanks to your generosity\, we also raised tens of thousands o
 f dollars to keep that work going! If you’d still like to support CLC\, 
 you can make a gift here.\nWe are deeply grateful to our Lead Sponsor\, In
 stitute on Aging\, and our Legacy Sponsors\, AT&T\, On Lok\, Deborah Satte
 n\, and Valorie & Dr. Leopoldo Villela\, along with all of our Community L
 eader and Benefactor sponsors who helped make the evening possible.\nEnjoy
  some pictures from the evening below.\n\nPublished by Community Living Ca
 mpaign\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1
 .0\n\nDetails: https://sfcommunityliving.org/event/bmt-startrek/?utm_sourc
 e=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\nSource: CalDi
 scovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022T214235Z
LOCATION:Virtual\, Activities Line (FY26-27)\, San Francisco\, CA\, United
  States
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sfcommunityliving.org/event/bmt-startrek/?utm_source=caldiscov
 ery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
