DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nComedy For Musicians Bu
 t Everyone Is Welcome\nFred Armisen\nTuesday\, October 27 | The Castro\n\n
 Fred Armisen is a comedian\, writer\, producer\, and musician. He is the c
 o-writer and co-star of IFC’s Emmy-nominated series Portlandia. He is in
  the hit Netflix series Wednesday as Uncle Fester. He stars in HBO’s Los
  Espookys\, which he co-wrote and executive produced. He can also be heard
  in the hit animated Super Mario Bros movie. Armisen stars in\, writes\, a
 nd produces IFC’s hit show Documentary Now. He has also appeared in HBO
 ’s Our Flag Means Death\, Judd Apatow’s The Bubble\, and Amazon’s se
 ries Forever. He voices characters in Big Mouth and The Mitchells vs. The 
 Machines. He is currently starring in the Broadway play All In. Armisen is
  an 11-season veteran of Saturday Night Live. From 2014-2024\, Armisen was
  band leader of the 8G Band on Late Night With Seth Meyers.\n\nall ages\nS
 old out\nAnother Planet Entertainment Presents: Comedy for Musicians But E
 veryone is Welcome - Three Nights!\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https
