BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Let's Go Lesbians!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T210000
DTSTAMP:20261021T214759Z
UID:dothebay-17979284@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Comedy
DESCRIPTION:Let's Go Lesbians! is Safe Words' October queer comedy showcas
 e at the Eagle: a sapphic\, Lesbian lineup built around sharp\, personal\,
  and unapologetically queer stand-up. Jenny Chalikian headlines\, and Tann
 a Samone Hall hosts.\n“Safe Words exists to create safe spaces for queer
  audiences and accelerate the careers of queer comedians.”\nTanna Samone
  Hall\nLesbian | She/Her | HOST\nTanna Samone is an SF Born Oakland raised
 \, comedian\, storyteller\, writer\, artist\, and educator. Her comedy der
 ives from her life experience growing up biracial and lesbian in the Bay. 
 She has performed at Safe Words\, Caribiner Comedy\, and hosts and produce
 s Comedy Q events.\n@tannasamone\nMicia Mosely\nLesbian | She/Her\nMicia M
 osely\, Ph.D. is a comedian and educator who keeps audiences learning & la
 ughing in a variety of contexts and venues. She performs her brand of soci
 al justice stand up comedy and hosts events all across the country. You ma
 y have seen her at The Laugh Factory in Chicago\, Gotham Comedy Club in NY
 \, Busboys and Poets in DC\; Comedy Oakland\, Brava Theater in S.F. Boston
  University\; U.C. Berkeley. NYU. SF Pride\; D.C. Black Pride or Girlfest 
 Hawaii. When she's not telling jokes she is working to transform schools w
