UID:dothebay-17960312@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:LOCATION\n\nGLBT Historical Society Museum\n\n4127 18th Street
 \n\nSan Francisco\, CA 94114\n\nADMISSION\n\n$10\; Free for GLBT Historica
 l Society Members\n\nDoors at 6:00 pm / Reading at 6:30 pm\n\nRSVP and res
 erve your tickets here\n\nPlease join the GLBT Historical Society and Crow
 ded Fire Theater as we jointly present the first of two staged readings of
  How to Live in a House on Fire\, a new play by Kari Barclay and directed 
 by M. Graham Smith.\n\nPresented for the first time in the San Francisco B
 ay Area where the story takes place\, this staged reading of a new play by
  performance scholar Kari Barclay looks to queer history as a lens to unde
 rstand our current moment of climate grief.\n\nAttendees to the program wi
 ll be treated with a live staged reading of the new play with a cast of ac
 tors\, followed by a talkback discussion with the creative team after the 
 show and an opportunity to share audience feedback and participate in the 
 development process!\n\nHOW TO LIVE IN A HOUSE ON FIRE asks how we care fo
 r each other in moments of crisis. It builds on a quote from Tennessee Wil
 liams: "We live in a perpetually burning building\, and what we must save 
 from it\, all the time\, is love."\n\nThe Chateau Homosexuel is a gay comm
 une on the brink of collapse. It's 1970 in Berkeley\, California\, and as 
 characters bicker over the future of gay liberation\, Benny and Jeremy are
  falling in love. When they try to decide what to do with an eviction noti
 ce\, suddenly something starts burning in the oven. Smoke fills the...\n\n
 $10\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://glbthistory.ticketing.veevar
 tapp.com/tickets/view/list/performance-talkback-how-to-live-in-a-house-on-
 fire-staged-reading-series\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5
 /performance-talkback-how-to-live-in-a-house-on-fire-staged-reading-series
 -tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
