BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Robert Shields: My Life as a Robot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17882159@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Robert Shields: My Life as a Robot celebrates the extraordinar
 y\, and often invisible\, impact one artist can have on the world. In the 
 1970s\, Robert Shields began performing his signature robot routine outsid
 e the Hollywood Wax Museum before later moving to street performances in S
 an Francisco’s Union Square. Within a few short years\, he and his wife\
 , Lorene Yarnell\, were headlining their own hit CBS variety series\, The 
 Shields & Yarnell Show. What Robert didn’t fully realize at the time was
  that his robot would go on to influence the DNA of popping\, locking\, an
 d hip-hop dance as we know it today.\n\nFunny\, joyful\, and full of genui
 ne wonder\, the film introduces you to a man who makes you believe anythin
 g is possible — including\, as Robert demonstrates\, street skiing throu
 gh downtown San Francisco.\n\nFollowed by a live performance by Poppin Joh
 n\; a Q&A with Robert Shields\, director Mark Bonn\, producer Christine Se
 ibert Bonn\, and Poppin John\, moderated by Peter L. Stein\; and a post-sc
 reening reception in the lobby.\n\nInfo and tickets: https://sfdancefilmfe
 st.org/fall-festival-2026/robert-shields/\n\n$25-45\n2026 SF Dance Film Fe
 stival:\n\nTickets: https://sfdancefilmfest.org/fall-festival-2026/robert-
 shields/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/robert-shields-my
 -life-as-a-robot-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7526148;-122.4078356
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34611227/dbcb1877-9a98-4fac-9345-63e6a7eeccf7.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Brava Theater\, 2781 24th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/robert-shields-my-life-as-a-robo
 t-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:San Francisco Bike Party (First Fridays)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1635276@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Sports Fitness
DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Bike Party (First Fridays)\nSan Francisco Bike P
 arty\nSan Francisco Bike Party (not to be confused with Critical Mass) is 
 a monthly celebration of biking for riders of different ages\, types\, and
  skill levels to enjoy. Every month is a different theme and you’re enco
 uraged to dress up.\nSan Francisco Bike Party is held on the first Friday 
 at 8:00 pm every month (meet at 7:30p\, roll at 8p). The starting location
  and route also changes every month. Check SF Bike Party’s Facebook page
  for updates.\nThe rides are fun and safe with stops to dance and socializ
 e along the way. You’ll follow planned routes exploring all different pa
 rts of the city each month. They encourage people to bring positivity and 
 contribute to good times while being respectful to others.\n\nWho runs it?
  Created by a co-op\, by and for bike enthusiasts\, run by volunteers who 
 plan the routes\, test ride them\, help participants ride in control\, avo
 id traffic disruption\, and not get lost. How SFBP rides: – Stay in the 
 right lane – Stop at red lights – Leave no trace – Ride predictably 
 and in control – Roll past conflict – Ride prepared – When in doubt\
 , “bike party!!”\nUpdated 5/6/22 – Event info last checked via Faceb
 ook and Instagram\n\nUpcoming San Francisco Bike Party (First Fridays) Eve
 nts\nFri 11/6 San Francisco Bike Party (First Fridays)Fri 12/4 San Francis
 co Bike Party (First Fridays)Disclaimer: Please double check event informa
 tion with the event organizer as events can be canceled\, details can chan
