DESCRIPTION:SF’s Winter “Renegade Craft Fair” at Fort Mason (Nov. 14
 -15)\nRenegrade Craft\nRenegade San Francisco Winter Craft Fair 2026 retur
 ns to Fort Mason Center Festival Pavilion on November 14 + 15\, 2026\, for
  a weekend of holiday shopping featuring 250+ curated artists and independ
 ent small businesses.\nBrowse handmade gifts and creative finds\, includin
 g ceramics\, apparel\, jewelry\, home goods\, accessories\, art\, and more
 . With independent makers from around the country\, it’s a great spot to
  find something more original than the usual holiday gifts.\nAdmission is 
 free\, with a suggested $5 contribution payable via QR code onsite. Contri
 butions support Renegade Craft’s mission to make its fairs accessible wh
 ile helping independent artists and creative small businesses thrive.\n\nR
 ain or shine: The fair is held indoors\, with food trucks and additional f
 eatures outdoors.\nFood and drinks: Food trucks and other food and coffee 
 options are available. You can also bring your own food and nonalcoholic b
 everages.\nAccessibility: The Festival Pavilion is at ground level\, with 
 a wheelchair-accessible elevator to the mezzanine. Most of the fair and al
 l restrooms are on the ground floor.\nGetting there: Carpooling\, rideshar
 es\, biking\, and public transit are encouraged. On Sunday\, November 15\,
  Marina Boulevard will be closed from 6:30 am to 11:30 am\, so expect alte
 rnate directions into Fort Mason and possible congestion.\nAnimals: Servic
 e animals are welcome.\n\n2026 Schedule:\nSaturday\, November 14\, 11 am t
 o...\n\n$5.00\n\nTickets: https://www.renegadecraft.com/fair/san-francisco
 -winter/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-winter-renegade-craft-fair-
 at-fort-mason-nov-14-15-2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
