BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:El Grupo de Apoyo Latino
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-16897784@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:LGBTQ
DESCRIPTION:El Grupo de Apoyo Latino de SFAF es un grupo social y educativ
 o que ofrece un espacio abierto\, seguro\, y confidencial para apoyar a la
  comunidad Latina afectada por el VIH y SIDA. Es un grupo diverso\, donde 
 el respeto es la base para que todos los asistentes puedan expresar librem
 ente sus experiencias\, identidad\, étnicidad\, nacionalidad\, sexualidad
 \, y creencias religiosas.\n\nTodas las reuniones son en español y se lle
 van a cabo en un ambiente positivo\, familiar\, y confidencial. Ven a comp
 artir con nosotros\, estamos seguros que encontrarás apoyo y recibirás i
 nformación para mejorar tu calidad de vida.\n\nSFAF ofrece servicios a cu
 alquier persona sin importar su situación migratoria.\n\nPara mas informa
 ción sobre El Grupo\, llama al 415-632-9722.\n\n_____\n\nOur support grou
 p\, El Grupo\, has been a stable source of family and community for Latino
 s\, Latinas and their families since the early 1980s. Join us for informat
 ion about sexual health and harm reduction\, meals and social support\, an
 d help finding health and social services.\n\nMeetings are in-person at 94
 0 Howard St Group Room A every Thursday from 3 to 5 pm.\n\nTickets: https:
 //www.sfaf.org/event/el-grupo-de-apoyo-latino/2026-11-19/\nDetails: https:
 //dothebay.com/events/2026/11/19/el-grupo-de-apoyo-latino-tickets\nSource:
  DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/29927226/cb8a2375-b449-442b-9bd1-c1948987613b.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:San Francisco AIDS Foundation\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/19/el-grupo-de-apoyo-latino-ticket
 s
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Clift Royal Sonesta Hotel Continues Its Speaker Series: Making
  History Fun Again
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T190000
DTSTAMP:20261023T050002Z
UID:dothebay-17973354@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:The Clift Royal Sonesta Hotel\, a San Francisco landmark since
  1915\, continues its monthly speaker series\, Making History Fun Again\, 
 with “San Francisco’s Media Evolution\,” a conversation with journal
 ists and media leaders who have helped tell the city’s stories across ge
 nerations and platforms.\nOn Thursday\, November 19\, Heather Knight\, San
  Francisco bureau chief for The New York Times\, will moderate a panel fea
 turing Will Hearst\, editor and publisher of Alta Journal\; award-winning 
 television journalist Wendy Tokuda\; political reporter Joe Fitzgerald Rod
 riguez of The San Francisco Standard\; and radio host and political commen
 tator John F. Rothmann.\nFrom newspaper dispatches to television broadcast
 s\, radio conversations and news delivered through smartphones\, San Franc
 isco’s media have chronicled a city defined by reinvention. Earthquakes\
 , local politics\, cultural movements\, housing challenges and unforgettab
 le personalities have provided generations of journalists with stories tha
 t resonate far beyond the Bay Area.\nBringing together perspectives from p
 rint\, television\, digital news and radio\, the evening will explore how 
 the city’s stories reach audiences\, how journalism has changed and what
  endures as new technologies reshape the media landscape. Guests will hear
  from people who have brought Bay Area news into homes\, onto doorsteps\, 
 over the airwaves and into the palm of a hand.\nThe complimentary event be
 gins with non-hosted cocktails at 5:00 p.m.\, followed by the program fro.
 ..\n\nFree\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/19/the-clift-ro
 yal-sonesta-hotel-continues-its-speaker-series-making-history-fun-again-ti
 ckets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/clif
 t-royal-sonesta-hotel-speaker-series-making-history-fun-5/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35039363/19cbc405-630b-473f-bfc2-09dceabbf96a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T050002Z
LOCATION:The Clift Royal Sonesta Hotel\, 495 Geary Street\, San Francisco\
 , CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/19/the-clift-royal-sonesta-hotel-c
 ontinues-its-speaker-series-making-history-fun-again-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Art Loop: “Waterfront Walkabout” Free SF Art Stroll (Embar
 cadero)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1636355@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Big Art Loop: “Waterfront Walkabout” Free SF Art Stroll (E
 mbarcadero)\nPoster Art by Hollis Callas\n\nSan Francisco’s new event se
 ries where live music\, interactive pop-ups\, & monumental art set the sta
 ge for a bayside stroll like no other!\n\nLaunching September 17 and retur
 ning monthly every third Thursday this fall\, Waterfront Walkabout is a fr
 ee series inviting you to experience the Big Art Loop – Portside as the 
 Embarcadero waterfront comes to life!\nDate: Thursday\, Sept 17\, 2026\nTi
 me: 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM\nLocation: Pier 14 to the Exploratorium\n\nOur eve
 nt is a series 3 events in the fall. The event will be taking place every 
 third Thursday of each month. September 17\, October 15th\, and November 1
 9th.\nWHAT TO EXPECT\nSoak in live music\, fresh oysters\, and drinks at t
 he Ferry Building’s front plaza\, then stroll the art trail to discover 
 playful pop-up experiences at four larger-than-life sculptures:\nCorpus (P
 ier 14): Step up to the glowing Shrimp Boat Art Car for beats by the bay\n
 Echoes (Ferry Terminal Plaza): Grab a paintbrush for outdoor Paint & Sip o
 r join interactive games with Playful SF and Chamber of Connection\n🧜 C
 oralee (Pier 1/2): Dive into mermaid crafts and enchanting water spirit st
 orytelling with En2Action\n️ Got Framed (Pier 7): Strike a pose on the p
 ier for free professional portraits\nGUIDED ART TOURS\nExplore at your own
  pace\, or join a free docent-led tour for a deeper dive into the stories 
 behind the four featured sculptures! These 60-minute guided walks depart f
 rom...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/waterfront-walkabo
 ut-free-sf-art-stroll-tickets-1998986624806?aff=oddtdtcreator&amp\;keep_tl
 d=true\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/big-art-loop-waterfront-walkabout
 -free-sf-art-stroll-embarcadero-2/\nSource: Funcheap SF
