BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New People: An Eye for an Eye
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T173000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17866475@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:This screening will take place at NEW PEOPLE CINEMA\, located 
 at 1746 Post Street in Japantown.\n\nDirector Tanaz Eshaghian in person fo
 r a post-screening Q&A\n\nAn Eye for an Eye unfolds like a real-life court
 room thriller\, with stakes as high as life and death. Years after killing
  her abusive husband in an act of self-defense\, Tahereh now faces executi
 on unless she can pay the Diya—blood money demanded by her abuser’s fa
 mily. With the clock ticking and public sympathy running low\, her son Moh
 sen is thrust into a desperate race against time to save his mother’s li
 fe\, turning to outside donors in a society where victims of domestic abus
 e are often met with silence—or scorn. With unprecedented access to priv
 ate negotiations\, legal proceedings\, and intimate family moments\, the f
 ilmmakers bring us deep inside a harrowing moral and legal labyrinth. We w
 itness not only the emotional toll on Tahereh and her children\, but also 
 the chilling mechanics of a justice system shaped by patriarchal values an
 d religious law. Gripping and deeply human\, An Eye for an Eye lays bare t
 he personal costs of systemic injustice—and the fierce resilience of a f
 amily fighting for their right to move forward.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 24m\n\nYe
 ar\n\n2025\n\nDirector\n\nTanaz Eshaghian\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nU
 nited States / Denmark / Iran\n\nLanguage\n\nFarsi with English Subtitles\
 n\nFirst Showing\n\nNovember 29\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nNew People Cinema\
 n\n\,\n\nFeatured\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/
 22133?siteToken=b6y5tsmq2ayrxb4ymw2rah8wy0\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/
 events/2026/11/29/new-people-an-eye-for-an-eye-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34538615/f6085590-baf1-419a-86e0-c8d62ee78b83.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/29/new-people-an-eye-for-an-eye-ti
 ckets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tokyo Godfathers (Subtitled)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T161500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T181500
DTSTAMP:20261023T171442Z
UID:dothebay-17979567@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Presented in Japanese with English subtitles\n\nIn modern-day 
 Tokyo\, three homeless people’s lives are changed forever when they disc
 over a baby girl at a garbage dump on Christmas Eve. As the New Year fast 
 approaches\, these three forgotten members of society band together to sol
 ve the mystery of the abandoned child and the fate of her parents. Along t
 he way\, encounters with seemingly unrelated events and people force them 
 to confront their own haunted pasts\, as they learn to face their future\,
  together.\n\nCo-written by Keiko Nobumoto (Cowboy Bebop) and featuring a 
 whimsical score by Keiichi Suzuki\, TOKYO GODFATHERS is a masterpiece by t
 urns heartfelt\, hilarious\, and highly original\, a tale of hope and rede
 mption in the face of seemingly insurmountable odds. (GKIDS)\n\nTickets: h
 ttps://drafthouse.com/sf/show/tokyo-godfathers-subtitled?cinemaId=0802&ses
 sionId=22962\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/29/tokyo-godfat
 hers-subtitled-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35067888/ac58f289-d1ba-412d-b914-b88229d56763.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T171442Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/29/tokyo-godfathers-subtitled-tick
 ets
