SUMMARY:Cameron Winter at Carnegie Hall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T211500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T231500
DTSTAMP:20261017T204148Z
UID:dothebay-17963784@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Late Screening!\n\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents\n\nA 
 Janus Films and Criterion Release\nCameron Winter at Carnegie Hall\nDirect
 ed by Paul Thomas Anderson\nPresented in 35mm\n\nWednesday\, December 2 | 
 The Castro\n\nCameron Winter\, in December 2025\, after a months-long sold
 -out tour with his band Geese\, returned to New York to play a single show
  at Carnegie Hall. This is the movie.\n\nDirected and shot on 35mm and 16m
 m by Oscar-winning filmmaker Paul Thomas Anderson (One Battle After Anothe
 r)\, the crew includes filmmaker and actor Benny Safdie (The Smashing Mach
 ine) and music producer Ariel Rechtshaid (Grammy winner for albums with Va
 mpire Weekend and Adele).\n\nGQ praised Cameron Winter’s show at Carnegi
 e Hall as “staggeringly good\,” and Nick Cave said he has a “a glori
 ous\, emotive voice with brilliant\, blistering words\, a racked and wondr
 ous thing.” Winter’s solo album Heavy Metal was named one of the best 
 of the year by Pitchfork\, Rolling Stone\, Paste and Mojo and Geese’s la
 st record Getting Killed was named the best album of 2025 by The New Yorke
 r\, NME\, and Stereogum.\n\nAll Ages\nSold out\nAnother Planet Entertainme
 nt presents\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://thecastro.com/events
 /cameron-winter-at-carnegie-hall-261202-late\nDetails: https://dothebay.co
 m/events/2026/12/2/cameron-winter-at-carnegie-hall\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34996187/ca767591-8ed0-46d3-ac29-2ddb5d3fc3c1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261017T204148Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/2/cameron-winter-at-carnegie-hall
END:VEVENT
